# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#162's comment, P48), L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees: broker is of unit any, priced by pxp,
# keyed by currencies; move buy writes a leg of unit etf into it, which currencies doesn't hold: LOAD-KEY at load,
# whatever the asks read (a reads n alone). 2.1.7's refcore loaded it clean and gave a hole where value read it.
# tally 2.2 (CHANGES.md 2.2-1): a kind of unit any is an outside kind only, so this one is marked outside.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit etf "fund unit"
kind brokerages: place any min 0 priced pxp outside
kind buys: event certain
  leg u: etf
place broker: brokerages lives 2026-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pxp[u in currencies]: num PLN/u
input d: date
input q: num etf
input n: int

move buy: buys
  on d
  leg u from market to broker amount q

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d = 2026-02-01 "s"
  q = 3 etf "s"
  n = 1 "s"

ask a: n
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY broker is priced by pxp, keyed by currencies, which holds neither broker nor etf (m.tally:10)
